  "concept": {
    "movement": "A watchful marsh bird with slower high steps and half-open wings held for balance; a deliberate long beak thrust. Deliberate alternating steps, visible knee and hock articulation, stable toe contact and restrained wings. The faster gait lengthens and quickens the steps without turning into flight.",
    "attack": "A short neck recoil into a long forward and downward beak stab, with both feet planted, then a quick recovery.",
    "death": "A forward breast-first collapse. The long neck folds, the legs release behind the body and the feather skirt settles without a beak-supported hover."
